<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Justin II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 520–578</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Justin II was Byzantine emperor from 565 to 578, nephew and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a>. He refused payments to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, and his reign saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 568 and a renewed war with Persia in which the fortress of Dara fell in 573. After losing his sanity he made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> II his co-ruler in 574. Embassies from the Nubian kingdoms reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> during his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/justin-ii.jpg" alt="Justin II" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Artemide Aste · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solidus_of_Justin_II_(obverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
